 {
  "repo": "customics",
  "name": "v0.1.0",
  "tagName": "v0.1.0",
  "publishedAt": "2026-07-02T14:17:11Z",
  "url": "https://github.com/prism-oncology/customics/releases/tag/v0.1.0",
  "descriptionHTML": "<h2>v0.1.0 — First public release 🎉</h2>\n<p>The API now runs entirely on <strong><a href=\"https://mudata.readthedocs.io/\" rel=\"nofollow\">MuData</a></strong> (<a href=\"https://scverse.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">scverse</a>): one object per omics source, clinical data in<br>\n<code>.obs</code>/<code>.uns</code>, and a scikit-learn-style <code>fit</code> / <code>predict</code> / <code>evaluate</code> workflow.</p>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MuData-native pipeline</strong> — the whole model (data loading, training, inference,<br>\nexplainability) now works directly on <code>MuData</code> objects.</li>\n<li><strong>Data helpers</strong> — <code>toy_dataset</code>, <code>prepare_input</code>, <code>get_shared_samples</code>,<br>\n<code>get_sub_mudata</code>, and <code>split_mudata</code> (one-call train/val/test split).</li>\n<li><strong>Visualization</strong> — <code>plot_cohort_overview</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Documentation</strong> — getting-started guide, API reference, and end-to-end tutorial.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Python ≥ 3.11</li>\n</ul>",
  "isPrerelease": false
 },
 {
